    "description": "SpaceWasm is a flight-compliant implementation of the WebAssembly (Wasm 1.0) specification for interpreting Wasm binaries onboard spacecraft, developed at NASA JPL Robotics. It is the interpreter behind F´'s Svc::WasmSequencer (F´ v4.4.0). Each module runs in its own sandbox with a fixed interface to flight software, a bounded instruction budget, and memory-safety traps, so autonomy and command sequencing code can be updated without risking safety-critical flight software. It streams and validates Wasm in fixed memory, and targets flight processors including ARM and RISC-V.",
